# Build and run artefacts.
#
# The two entries that matter most are `models/` and `.venv/`: the local NLLB
# model is 617 MiB and the virtual environment is a few hundred MiB more, so a
# careless `git add .` would commit the better part of a gigabyte and the whole
# repository would become impractical to clone. Everything else here is
# regenerable.

# --- Python prototype ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# The virtual environment is machine specific: paths, compiled extensions and the
# interpreter version. `prototype/requirements.txt` is the reproducible record.
.venv/
venv/

# --- local models ---
# Fetched by prototype/fetch_model.py; the download is resume-safe and documented,
# which is a better distribution mechanism than a binary in the history.
models/

# --- generated outputs ---
build/
dist/

# --- measurement output (written by --stats-json and the benchmark tools) ---
stats.json
*.stats.json
bench_*.json

# --- editor / OS ---
# `.vscode/settings.json` is deliberately NOT shared. VS Code reads it from the
# workspace, so committing it hands every cloner this machine's terminal
# auto-approve allowlist, plus absolute paths containing a local username
# (C:/Users/<name>/...). `extensions.json` is the one file that is genuinely
# useful to share, since it only recommends extensions.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
